{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the presence of a sure outcome in each lottery and prefers the lottery that offers a sure outcome. In this decision problem, Lottery A offers 1500 Euros with 100% probability, which is a sure outcome. Lottery B offers either 3000 Euros or -3000 Euros, each with 50% probability, meaning it has no sure outcome. Therefore, the decision reason can be applied: Lottery A contains a sure outcome, Lottery B does not, and the reason would prefer Lottery A.",
